  - label: "Why visit Beijing?"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/dest-beijing.png" alt="Beijing" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">北<br/>&#28216;</div></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Culture & History</span><h2 class="display-h2">Why visit Beijing?</h2><p>China's capital for most of the past eight centuries, Beijing is where imperial grandeur meets modern ambition. The Forbidden City, the Great Wall, the Temple of Heaven — these are icons the world knows. But the city's real magic hides in its hutong alleyways, its dawn tai chi gatherings, and its dumpling restaurants that have changed nothing in 150 years.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Iconic experiences in Beijing"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Must-See Sights</span><h2 class="display-h2">Iconic experiences in Beijing</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>The Forbidden City</h3><p>The world's largest palace complex — 980 buildings, 500 years of emperors, and golden roofs that glow at dusk. Our scholar-guides bring 600 years of drama to life.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>The Great Wall at Mutianyu</h3><p>Skip the tourist crowds at Badaling. We take you to a quieter, fully restored section at dawn — you may have the wall to yourself for an hour.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Temple of Heaven</h3><p>Where Ming emperors prayed for good harvests. Arrive early to see locals practicing tai chi, singing opera, and flying kites.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>The Hutongs</h3><p>Cycle or walk through Beijing's ancient courtyard neighborhoods. Visit a local family for a home-cooked dumpling dinner.</p></div></div></div></section>
